# tests/CPR_DIFF_ALLOWLIST — Known signature parity divergences between
# --emit-ir (direct codegen) and --use-ir-codegen (typed Sprout-IR).
#
# Each entry is a function name (with leading `@`) whose intersection-side
# signatures are PERMITTED to differ between the two codegen paths. The
# scripts/cpr_differential_check.sh framework reports allowlisted divergences
# as warnings but does not fail.
#
# Format: one `@<name>` per line, optional `# justification` after the name.
# Lines starting with `#` are comments. Blank lines ignored.
#
# Adding an entry MUST include a clear justification:
#   - WHY the divergence is benign for the calling convention
#   - WHAT it would take to close the gap (so a future PR can clear it)
#
# When a divergence is closed (both paths emit the same signature), remove
# the entry. CI will fail with "unexpected closure" so removal cannot drift.

@sprout_abort_match  # noreturn attribute drift: typed path declares with `noreturn`, direct path without. Benign for ABI (calling convention is `void()` either way; noreturn is an optimization hint). Closing needs FnSig type to carry attributes — ~50-line codegen.sprout refactor; out of scope for the differential framework PR.
@str_compare  # i64-vs-ptr arg drift: typed path declares `@str_compare(i64, i64)` (correct — the C runtime sig is `long long str_compare(long long, long long)`); direct codegen declares `@str_compare(ptr, ptr)` via emit_ptr_comparison's shared ptr-coercion. Benign on all current targets (ptr and i64 share the same general-purpose argument registers on x86-64 / ARM64). The typed path is the correct side. Closing it means fixing direct codegen's emit_ptr_comparison to pass i64 for str_compare while keeping ptr for str_eq (they share a coercion today) — tracked in BACKLOG §1; codegen.sprout is deleted at the PR 13 dispatcher flip, which also closes this.
